  "source": {
    "title": "Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\": Armagh); party labels from the nominations in the Belfast News-Letter, 9 January 1899, p. 7",
    "publisher": "Belfast News-Letter (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure read from the page image; labels from the nominations report"
  },
  "note": "St. Patrick's, or North, Ward; poll on Monday 16 January 1899, declared near midnight, \"the first six -- all Nationalists -- being elected\". Of the 23 candidates, six were selected by the Nationalist Association and six were Unionists; the rest were described as nominated by practical jokers, mostly without their knowledge. George Sherry's own label is lost in the nominations report; the result report counts him among the Nationalists. Eliza Hillock, Elizabeth M'Glone and Mary Brown carry no label."
